I fixed #1169. The banner, /git stage and /git status now read git's first changed file correctly.

Cause: run_git and run_git_in_dir in src/git.rs called .trim() on git's output. That removed the leading space on the first line of git status --porcelain, so  M Cargo.toml became M Cargo.toml. That line then read as a staged change, and its path came out as argo.toml.

Fix: both helpers now go through one new function, git_stdout, which trims only the end of git's output. Error messages are still trimmed on both ends.

Who else reads this output: I went through all 134 hits from git grep 'run_git(\|run_git_in_dir(' src. Four kinds of output can start with a space, and the old trim made every one of them wrong:
• status --porcelain / --short (the banner, /git status, /git stage, /diff, context.rs)
• diff --stat
• branch --list -a
• show <rev>:<path>, which used to lose a file's leading blank lines before being compared with the file on disk

No caller needed the leading trim. Outputs that are a single token (shas, rev-parse, ls-files) are unaffected. I checked that log --pretty=format: --name-only doesn't start with a blank line. So /git status, /git branch, /diff --stat and the context.rs reader are fixed without editing those files.

Tests: I added src/git_porcelain_tests.rs. It runs real git in a temp directory through run_git_in_dir, so it passes the rule that all git calls go through src/git.rs. It covers:
• two unstaged edits → 0 staged / 2 modified, with both full paths
• a one-character filename a on the first line survives
• near-miss: a staged-only first line M  x still counts as staged
• the first line of --short and --stat keeps its space

At the old trim(), the four bug tests failed on the missing space and the near-miss passed. After the fix all five pass.

Gate: cargo fmt --check, clippy with -D warnings and the full cargo test all pass. The test run hit two repo checks along the way, and I fixed both:
• the git chokepoint check: the test setup now goes through run_git_in_dir
• the orphan-module check: the module is now named after its file

Run against the built binary (after cargo build had finished, binary mtime 23:46:29), in a temp repo with two unstaged edits:
• the banner shows · 2 modified
• /git status shows  M Cargo.toml /  M src/lib.rs
• /git stage lists 1. [M] Cargo.toml  2. [M] src/lib.rs

I also raised the size cap for src/git.rs from 2032 to 2037 lines in tests/module_size.rs, and added a CHANGELOG entry.

There are two commits. The main body says the new function adds 1 line; it adds 2. A follow-up commit (c986d4c2) corrects that in the module_size.rs comment, but the first commit's text still has the wrong number. Neither is pushed, so the commits can still be squashed if you want that fixed.
